(superhero.id)` grouped by `publisher_name`.\n- **Average Height of Superheroes:** `AVG(height_cm)`.\n- **Superpower Prevalence:** `COUNT(hero_power.hero_id)` grouped by `power_name`.\n- **Attribute Ranking:** `RANK() OVER (ORDER BY attribute_value DESC)` for specific attributes like Strength or Speed.\n- **Gender Distribution:** `COUNT(superhero.id)` grouped by `gender`.\n\n### Calculation Logic\n- **Percentage Calculation:** `MULTIPLY(DIVIDE(SUM(condition), COUNT(total)), 100)`.\n- **Difference Calculation:** `SUBTRACT(SUM(condition1), SUM(condition2))`.\n- **Ratio Calculation:** `DIVIDE(SUM(condition1), SUM(condition2))`.\n\n## 4. Constraints & Conventions\n\n### Filtering Criteria\n- **Publisher Filtering:** Use `publisher_name` for filtering superheroes by publisher.\n- **Superpower Filtering:** Use `power_name` for filtering superheroes by superpower.\n- **Attribute Filtering:** Use `attribute_name` and `attribute_value` for filtering based on specific attributes.\n\n### Temporal Boundaries\n- **Fiscal Year Format:** YYYY-MM-DD for all date-related entries.\n\n### Unit Conversions\n- **Height:** Always recorded in centimeters.\n- **Weight:** Always recorded in kilograms.\n\n### Currency Formatting\n- Not applicable as the database does not contain financial data.\n\n## 5. Exemplar Use Cases\n\n### Example 1: Superpower Prevalence\n- **Natural Language:** Determine how many superheroes possess the superpower \"Flight.\"\n- **SQL:** `SELECT COUNT(hero_power.hero_id) FROM hero_power INNER JOIN superpower ON hero_power.power_id = superpower.id WHERE superpower.power_name = 'Flight'`\n\n### Example 2: Average Height Calculation\n- **Natural Language:** Calculate the average height of superheroes published by Marvel Comics.\n- **SQL:** `SELECT AVG(height_cm) FROM superhero INNER JOIN publisher ON superhero.publisher_id = publisher.id WHERE publisher.publisher_name = 'Marvel Comics'`\n\n### Example 3: Gender Distribution\n- **Natural Language:** Count the number of male superheroes.\n- **SQL:** `SELECT COUNT(superhero.id) FROM superhero INNER JOIN gender ON sup",
